  Easy names at home

  ╭───────────────╮      ╭────────╮      ╭────────────────────────────────╮
  │ phones        │──────│ router │──────│ Caddy                          │
  │ TVs · laptops │      ╰───┬────╯      │ jellyfin.192-168-1-20.sslip.io │
  ╰───────────────╯      internet ✗      ╰────────────────────────────────╯

  Open each App by name instead of a port number. Caddy answers the names on your home network.
  The addresses with numbers keep working if a name doesn't.

  Which names?
  Each App with a web page gets a name like jellyfin.192-168-1-20.sslip.io. Names are checked from
  this computer, not your phone or TV; their name lookup may differ. No .local names are
  announced.

  When names don't work
  The names need internet name lookup. Some routers hide them, and a phone using its own name
  lookup may behave differently. Use the addresses with numbers when a name fails.

  If your network address changes
  The names contain this computer's network address. If your router changes it, old bookmarks stop
  working. Review the LAN address in Settings. Ask your router to keep the same address to avoid
  this.


